    98	
    99	Seln had the blank sheet in front of him, and he did not write on it, but he laid one finger on it where the fifth line would have gone, and the table watched him do it, and understood that the pattern had its fifth point and that the pattern was now a shape, and that the man at the table's end had known its shape since the second session and had been waiting, per his trade, for the shape to draw itself.
