editions/monroe-1.3/book-05-the-silver-standard/packets/MOVEMENT-007.md:11:> **[Coordinator note 2026-10-05, after M6 close — governs over this packet's dates.]** Calendar per BOOK_MAP §6 [M6-redated]: ring complete dawn T11; Shield captain T11; duelist T14 (three days later), Vastin sits T14; rest day/birthday T15; team trial T16. Seln's "nine days" below reads "thirteen days". The Silver exhibitions are in the **main floor's ring** (built on the main floor after the brackets cleared it), not "the second floor". Lira is on half work for her LEFT shoulder from T9 for a week. Ternhall's lattice anchors are PROVISIONAL house doctrine (M6).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-05-the-silver-standard/packets/MOVEMENT-007.md:26:- **The chair fills between the bouts.** Vastin is in inspection greys, alone. He writes twice and leaves before the number. **Vastin cutaway (~1,500)** afterward: what he wrote twice, in his own words, and why he did not wait for the rating. No conclusion, no threat; the reports have stopped being the thing that matters. Seln at the table: "The office notes that the chair was held for him for nine days before he sat in it … Somebody announced it for him."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-05-the-silver-standard/packets/MOVEMENT-007.md:38:Development: about 15 Cael beats (the midpoint pole is the largest). Supporting: Lira (2), Brom (1–2), Karis (2), Seln (1–2), Ephram (2), Rooke (2), Withrow (1), Daeva (1, seen only).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-05-the-silver-standard/packets/MOVEMENT-007.md:43:- Hesk's book is given here and the inventory is written in it. Keep the old volume for daily road entries later (C6).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-05-the-silver-standard/packets/MOVEMENT-007.md:46:- Daeva: no conversation. The trial contact is a single exchange, and she stops for one second.
books/book-04-copper-crown/chapters/chapter-08.md:89:The seam was the story, and it was no longer a private one. Brom's flaw had been named honestly at Greyvane a year ago and had cost him nothing there, because Greyvane had not held anybody fast enough to reach it: the self-taught redirect carried a gap between reading an incoming force and executing against it, and inside that gap he was, briefly, an ordinary person standing still. Ephram had found the gap in three sessions — Cael had watched most of the fortnight that followed from the east hall's gallery, nine pages' worth — and by now the entire cohort had been taught to look for it.
books/book-04-copper-crown/chapters/chapter-08.md:133:Then he put the schedule against it. The session calendar gave each enrollee a bout about every nine days. A hundred and sixty days of season. Seventeen bouts, and that was if nobody was ever injured, deferred, or unmatched, which happened to everyone.
books/book-04-copper-crown/chapters/chapter-08.md:157:Ephram had said one thing to him all term, in the Crown yard, in front of enough people that it was clearly meant to be a posted position rather than a remark: *Greyvane needed him to be real. We don't. I'll wait for the semester evaluation.* Cael had written it down that night and had written *fair — same terms I'd offer* underneath it, and had meant both.
books/book-04-copper-crown/chapters/chapter-08.md:177:Nothing had moved in any of the five since Greyvane, which he wrote down as a line of its own, because a season in which nothing changed was still a fact about the architecture and deserved the same ink as a season in which everything did.
books/book-04-copper-crown/chapters/chapter-08.md:185:The first sentence was scheduling. The second was a prediction he was confident enough in to write down: Lira would take the Copper Crown, because there was nobody in that column who could hold her for eleven seconds let alone a final, and it would mean nothing about what she actually was, and the paper would still say Copper the morning after. Brom would lose bouts this season that he would not have lost at Greyvane, and every one of them would make him better, because Rooke's cohort was a curriculum and not a ceiling and Brom had spent a year mistaking one for the other.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/packets/MOVEMENT-008.md:24:- **What Leaving Costs**: three roads priced; the cache argued for and lost out loud; **Bracken brings Brom's finding at night** — Iron, found, and the guidance note — "How many boxes is your research?" / "Three." / "Then I'm carrying three boxes."; Lira's whole bill; Karis's forfeiture priced in bibliography order (the Greyvane request redirected to Hesk; the assistant's letter); Seln's one sentence; **Ephram brought in, told the departure and nothing of the cache, asks for one bout**; five hands, Seln's last. **Withrow** alone: the four days she knew and said nothing; the other column; **"The record will say you left…"**; she opens the door herself. **Lira's window** (~1.5k) that night.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/packets/MOVEMENT-009.md:25:- **The Registry Line**: what the road still had, day by day; the last chartered waystation and its keeper ("You've boxes."); the last tier notice with a hay sum; **the last watcher's nod to Brom**; **the last station** (swept; roof mended by someone; the book that stops four years ago with its open line); five crossings, each in a sentence; **"You couldn't read me… Thanks for the eleven seconds."**; the Line, unmarked; **"Nobody's watching."**; the first night outside any jurisdiction; **the reply to Daeva** sent west with the post-rider at the ford; "Both promises ride east with me."; the first ridge — **"Nobody mentions that it's big."**
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/packets/MOVEMENT-009.md:26:- **Nine**: the shelf above the unnamed valley; the watch argument; Brom's load rule; Karis's field archive; Lira's route sheet; money; Ephram's absence once; **the inventory — nine, the blank where a name would be**; the anomaly's shorter procedure; **"Reydan will get his answer. Daeva will get her rematch."**; **both poles left standing**; letters to Hesk and Vell with no return address; **the closing faceless window** and the new line; the last lines.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/packets/MOVEMENT-009.md:30:- Protected: "Your files are in order. All four."; "Doors open both ways."; Gault's note; the Seln image as the chapter's first sentence; *pending jurisdiction*; Cael's reply to Daeva; "Nobody's watching."; "…it's big."; the inventory; *Still open. Still real. Patience.*; the Reydan/Daeva line; both poles; *active non-compliance, observation priority escalated* (bible form); the closing exchange.
books/book-06-the-compacts-hand/chapters/chapter-18.md:29:She spoke for fifty-one minutes. She had a folder in front of her and she opened it once. She argued the text one last time, whole, from the keel up — the assay clause's own language, the enabling instrument behind it, the four hundred years of practice that had made it what it was — and she did the thing she had done since the Greyvane hearing, which was to build every proposition on a document already in the seat's hands, so that not one sentence of her closing asked the seat to take her word for anything.
books/book-06-the-compacts-hand/chapters/chapter-18.md:159:*So. Five weeks. Council tomorrow. Not to analyze the ruling. To make the decision the ruling was built to prevent us from making — the one Lira asked about in the first week, and Brom priced in three sentences, and Seln has been holding a locked case toward for fifteen years, and I have been refusing since Greyvane because I believed the text was ground.*
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/packets/MOVEMENT-004.md:13:Twelve days after the preliminary ruling, in the first term's middle weeks [B5-reconciled 2026-10-05: season word struck; audit A1]. Lira has put a note on the residence board: *small room, Fifth-day, after supper, five.* The pre-restriction inventory is complete in five offices. The Silver program's first road meet is close [B5-reconciled 2026-10-05: the confluence is the region's fourth meet "at the year's turn, in the deep cold" of a qualifying year; B6's year is not one (the cycle is three years), so this is the lighter, earlier card of a non-qualifying year — one line, stated once; no season word; audit B3].
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/packets/MOVEMENT-004.md:25:- **The escort order**: the lodge's posted board; Withrow requires it read aloud (eighty-one words); Bracken's minute forty on a seal he cannot place; the refusal; "voluntarily" aimed at an empty gallery; no written refusal demanded; the refectory by noon; **Rooke eats in the open seat**; Gault: "I have written that down."
books/book-06-the-compacts-hand/chapters/chapter-13.md:116:*Eight. Taken from someone the system sent namelessly, to hold me namelessly. Every other piece in this log has a person attached — Lira, Feryn, Brom, Reydan, Karis, Seln, Daeva. This one has a hand and no face. I finally own a piece of the machine itself. I don't know yet what that costs. Write it down anyway.*
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/packets/MOVEMENT-007.md:9:**Read before drafting:** this movement has no source chapter of its own. Read the threads it carries: source `chapter-09.md` (the *fled* default; both roads; the first box; the carters), `chapter-14.md` (Lira's three bouts; the qualification, defined at BOOK_MAP §4a as the registry's Silver advancement evaluation [B5-reconciled 2026-10-05: audit B9] [B5-reconciled 2026-10-06: on the page it is "the advancement evaluation" or "the sitting" (B5 ch20:231, ch21:63, ch60:145), never "qualification"; audit §F.3 B9]), `chapter-16.md` (the map), `chapter-18.md` (the year's documentary work; the counsel; Havel), `chapter-19.md` (the Greyvane request; the assistant; the docket; the second Velmere envelope unopened four weeks), `chapter-20.md` (the band Ephram charted), `chapter-22.md` (Seln east twice; water at forty paces; Brom checks). Context: `BOOK_MAP.md` §§2, 4a (M7 rows), 4d, 4e (#9–11), 6 (Lira, Havel, Vastin), 9; `STATE_LEDGER.md` (after M6).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/packets/MOVEMENT-003.md:7:- Owner names: canon names only (adds Vastin on the page, Ilsev, Umber, Daeva by document). Unnamed: Vastin's clerk, the northern junior evaluator, the counsel, the assistant, the press man, the correspondents, the haulage practitioner of Withrow's story.
