editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-001/compiled-prompt.md:365:He closed the year that evening in Hesk's book, at the table under the window, with Hesk's steel pen.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-001/compiled-prompt.md:385:*Daeva's storm. Taken in the middle of a fight she began, awake, by the old minute's three lines, with the cost on paper as far as paper went. Fifteen feet of it, a third deep. The first notice that ever said Gold. The first that ever warned me what it gave might not hold, and that part stands. Everything else I carry is still shifting to make room for it, slower than after any of the others. Gold is heavy. Hesk taught me to write down what a thing costs the instrument as well as what it does. So: written.*
