editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/STATE_LEDGER.md:636:- (c) The house hears of the denial (day 44) before Vastin receives it (day 45) — a new beat that keeps the spine's order (Halcenvane hears before the second sitting) inside the coordinator's calendar.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/STATE_LEDGER.md:637:- (d) Daeva's statement is set aside at the **third** sitting, not the second, so that the second sitting's fifty-one minutes stays an exhibits morning and the statement's rhyme with Vastin lands in the same room as the ruling.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/STATE_LEDGER.md:642:- (i) Vastin's cutaway is ~5,100 words (the packet's ~5k).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/STATE_LEDGER.md:646:- **Vastin's room (flag, minor):** the porter feeds the pigeons from the same half-circle; a **letter-book** of fair copies of everything that left the room in nineteen years; the lowest drawer at the far end of the cabinet of shallow drawers holds what is his; the floor's lamps go out at the half-bell after six (the house's rule); the candle on the consumables under his name.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/STATE_LEDGER.md:647:- **Vastin's clerk (flag):** nine years in the outer office; narrow, tidy; his one non-work sentence ("Will you be getting home tonight, sir? It's set in to rain.").
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/STATE_LEDGER.md:648:- **Vastin's two chapter-fourteen files (flag):** a hill station keeper whose cracked housing read every Ash a rank high for six years, covered by false returns; a coastal district officer paid to enter a rank no frame had read; the second's daughter's letter answered *no*.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/STATE_LEDGER.md:649:- **Vastin's four supplementary findings (flag):** a district's enrollment challenge (decisive against the district, which wrote without grievance), a hill station's frame (retired on his evidence), a guild hall's matter, a sponsorship quarrel — all received.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/STATE_LEDGER.md:651:- **The northern junior's file (flag — plant):** a young evaluator from the northern district; a station Kindling entry four years old for a young woman whose shown work runs ahead of it, within tolerance; *continue observation*; Vastin keeps the copy in *held*.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/STATE_LEDGER.md:652:- **Withrow (flag):** "form thirty, refusals, third series" in the registry's second-year drafting book; she taught it as a mercy to every junior; her haulier: Force, Bronze Rank Four, thirty-one, guild haulage contract in a river district, wife, son and daughter, fourteen years owing; a station clerk's slip twenty years before; two silent frames; seven weeks; nine letters from four offices brought in a flour sack on the fourth day; east past the last station in eighteen months; the daughter is M1's daughter at the counter.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/STATE_LEDGER.md:654:- **Bracken's post procedure (flag):** a second trestle; four chalked boards *HOUSES. SPONSORS. FACULTIES. OTHER.*; the daily count in his counter daybook; heaviest day 196; fourteen chartered houses answered in the same two lines (text in ch16); grey-sealed seat letters carried up by hand.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/STATE_LEDGER.md:663:- **The lodge (flag):** the lodge-man (grey beard, bad knee, kept the gate since before Bracken); the wing may read the arrivals book on the Seventh-day; **the road column**, a line every bell since "the year of the thieves", on the order of the chancellor before last; the carter and the gatepost.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/STATE_LEDGER.md:665:- **Daeva's statement header** (not protected; my text) and the Silver-and-above statement provision: forty-four recorded uses, all by Silvers, never a Gold; hers the forty-fifth.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/STATE_LEDGER.md:669:- **Honest floor (flag):** under low lamps the lane's running dust throws a shadow on the boards, so the lane can be seen as a moving dark band; Lira reads it and bursts along its edge. No new figure (the lane's bill stays ten counts).

