editions/monroe-1.3/book-05-the-silver-standard/packets/MOVEMENT-002.md:51:How much of each bout to stage and which to compress; the meet towns' texture (sheep-pen footings, the mill hall's racks and loading doors); the order of the mill-town days; conversation and humor at the inn tables; whether Rooke reviews on the steps or in the yard; the design details of the variance program.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-05-the-silver-standard/packets/MOVEMENT-007.md:11:> **[Coordinator note 2026-10-05, after M6 close — governs over this packet's dates.]** Calendar per BOOK_MAP §6 [M6-redated]: ring complete dawn T11; Shield captain T11; duelist T14 (three days later), Vastin sits T14; rest day/birthday T15; team trial T16. Seln's "nine days" below reads "thirteen days". The Silver exhibitions are in the **main floor's ring** (built on the main floor after the brackets cleared it), not "the second floor". Lira is on half work for her LEFT shoulder from T9 for a week. Ternhall's lattice anchors are PROVISIONAL house doctrine (M6).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-05-the-silver-standard/packets/MOVEMENT-007.md:26:- **The chair fills between the bouts.** Vastin is in inspection greys, alone. He writes twice and leaves before the number. **Vastin cutaway (~1,500)** afterward: what he wrote twice, in his own words, and why he did not wait for the rating. No conclusion, no threat; the reports have stopped being the thing that matters. Seln at the table: "The office notes that the chair was held for him for nine days before he sat in it … Somebody announced it for him."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-05-the-silver-standard/packets/MOVEMENT-007.md:43:- Hesk's book is given here and the inventory is written in it. Keep the old volume for daily road entries later (C6).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-05-the-silver-standard/packets/MOVEMENT-003.md:25:- **Karis's information audit** for the whole company: nothing tactical within thirty feet of a rail, letters through Bracken's pouch, "Decent and instrumental at once." Ephram's rehearsed entry was sold within a day.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-05-the-silver-standard/packets/MOVEMENT-003.md:31:- **Cael vs the grappler foreman (~2,800):** the designed slow first exchange meets a real grappler. One hand gets on him. Compression stays banked at contact. The left shoulder-seam is wrenched and he scrambles; then he wins the long way. "Paid full price, first installment." The shoulder takes four days. [B4-reconciled 2026-10-05: sided LEFT so it stays distinct from the right shoulder that pays the plate/Pressure (OWNER #36) and from Lira's Zerin "burst shoulder" in M6; audit C5.]
editions/monroe-1.3/book-04-copper-crown/packets/MOVEMENT-006.md:29:- **The final settles (new on the page).** **Lira vs Fiske, semifinal (Lira window ≈2,000 of a ≈3,000 fight):** four exchanges again, harder, and "one very long minute at the end that the first meeting had not needed." This is where the leading hip is damaged; the final runs on it. Fiske's knowledge of Lira is now complete, and Lira must win with less. One brief Fiske–Lira exchange after, with nothing said that reveals the future. **Brom vs Merrick (≈1,200)**, taken in the fifth. "Right." / "You're going to be unbearable about this." / "Now I get faculty supervision and a crowd." Karis: "It's the nineteenth."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-04-copper-crown/packets/MOVEMENT-006.md:30:- **No sparring for nine days.** Lira racks the batons: "I've beaten you nine times in two years and you've beaten me eleven… neither of us fights chess." Cael's sentence: "two Iron-equivalent practitioners who have never been allowed to fight anybody their own size." "Nine days. Nobody talks about hips."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-04-copper-crown/packets/MOVEMENT-008.md:22:- **Lira (cutaway, Ch51):** dawn, a hip that sets in two stages, Fenmark's hall in memory, and the north door. She cannot plan for his number and he cannot plan for hers; that was the point of nine days' silence. **Havel (cutaway):** a records officer off duty with nothing in his hands, choosing to be here.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-05-the-silver-standard/packets/MOVEMENT-001.md:54:The roster stands and the season is five days out. Cael holds a printed card he did not argue for, an instrument he wants honestly and has already decided to manage, and a silence above Vastin that he cannot see. The road to the first meet shows as a paler seam in the dark.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-05-the-silver-standard/packets/MOVEMENT-009.md:11:> **[Coordinator note 2026-10-05, after M6 close — governs over this packet's dates.]** Calendar per BOOK_MAP §6 [M6-redated] (OWNER-DECISIONS #41): finals day T24; panel overnight T24–25; the morning after and the meeting T25; closing ceremony T26; road home seventeen days. Do not state the tournament's length in days (the office's "three weeks" stands as the round figure).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-05-the-silver-standard/packets/MOVEMENT-009.md:13:> **[Coordinator note 2026-10-05, after M8 review — what M9 inherits.]** (1) THE RING (canon): fifty-two by forty-eight; the oak round the highest point; a half-inch fall from it to the barrier's foot every way (a dome; the long way, north to south, is the longest road downhill); a dry trench under an iron grating, "a hand and a half", falling slightly toward the east break; four masts at the quarters, each grounded twice into the trench, crown-of-nails heads; six-foot barrier with a bull-nose cap; four breaks, each with a cap seam felt through a boot; three rows of seats gone. Specification from Auremont's risk office at the house's expense. (2) FINALS DAY'S CARD: the three bracket finals (Iron, Silver, Gold) and the team-trial final (Auremont v the river academy) — place the trial final on the morning card; the match is the true event after them. Halcenvane is third on the continent "as the count stands at the close of the trials; to be confirmed at the closing". (3) DAEVA: Storm Path from her own side — asking the air, leaning, the road, the crooked lane, "let the air go slack" (the coastal veteran at fifteen) — her vocabulary stays hers, apart from Karis's fold / *permitted* / "arrives third". She told Cael what the masts are rated to, at the west mast (M8 ch52). She never theorizes what he is. (4) BODIES at T24: Cael fit, the hip and right-hand burn healed; a dull hold behind the eyes from deep recall on T23; the medium read narrows attention (Lira, Brom unheard). Brom's LEFT shoulder sore from the third-place trial, forearms taped. Karis's palms pink. Lira fit (the left arm held close is a habit). Ephram hoarse. (5) THE BANK, as minuted in Hesk's book on T23: Wind past six ("the bill comes in the morning"); the push from the Bronze at Ardenmere at fighting load past four blows a sitting; Reydan's give on a scored floor before a crowd, not since the Ardenmere bout; Karis's spark past the two contacts allowed in public; the read as far down as it goes. Shadow sealed for the debt; Seln never told why. (6) Vastin resolved to stay for the figure this time.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-05-the-silver-standard/packets/MOVEMENT-009.md:49:- Book 6 Ch1 handoff: Hesk's volume holds the year's ledger, and the road's daily entries close in the old volume's last leaves. The flag "stood eleven weeks" belongs to Book 6, so do not resolve it here. Watchers resume on the road. No season name for the road home or the recess ahead (#35). Vastin is the Archmarshal, no age.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-05-the-silver-standard/packets/MOVEMENT-009.md:55:Chapter boundaries (three for the match is the plan, but the author decides); every tactic inside §8's frame; the strata of the silence; the panel's arguments beyond the protected ruling; the morning's small breakages; the meeting's silences and counts; the ceremony's choreography; the road's days and talk; whether the optional Norhold session appears.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-04-copper-crown/STATE_LEDGER.md:12:- **Book 4 runs:** the final Greyvane term (≈5 months; Karis's find in week 3, the Edran rematch in week 20, Quenna in week 21, Prynn in week 22) → four days on the road → arrival at Halcenvane (five months and nine days after the ruling) → the season → **the eleventh of Sowing (Cael turns sixteen)** → the inspection, **the twelfth to the twenty-third of Reaping** (Copper final the 19th; semester evaluation the 20th; interview the 21st; departure the 23rd; file returned the 24th; quarterly drafted the 26th; corridor warning the 27th) → the first week of the month after Reaping (Lira's Arbiter evaluation) → term close → twelve-week recess (Book 5).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-04-copper-crown/STATE_LEDGER.md:148:**Calendar.** Greyvane final term: wk 3 the find (Thursday-ish afternoon); wk 4 nine letters; wk 7 first replies; wk 8 Bracken's first (four questions); wk 11 the fourth (forty-one); wk 14 Thursday night the finding, letter to Bracken next morning; wk 16 the other three file transfers; wk 17 the fifteenth letter; wk 19 counsel's seal to Naveth; wk 20 rematch (first bell); wk 21 Thursday Quenna; wk 22 Monday Naveth's notice, Wednesday Wray and packing, Thursday Prynn at the gate and departure. Four days' road. Arrival at Halcenvane = **five months and nine days after the ruling**. Then Halcenvane days 1–21: day 2 the rooms; day 3 the method failure and triage; day 6 the Crown yard; day 9 Brom assessed and placed, Ostrand; day 11 the log; day 13 the hatch; day 14 the faculty session (Rooke); about day 16 the carrel appeals; day 19 Withrow; day 21 the assessment notice. No season named at Halcenvane.
