editions/monroe-1.3/book-05-the-silver-standard/STATE_LEDGER.md:38:- **Cael:** the Power Log (the old volume, near its last leaves; Hesk's bound volume arrives at the rest day), the year's inventory closed on the last night of term with Hesk's steel drafting pen; the observation notebook, with Hesk's reply and the birthday note behind its front board; Vell's letter (five short sentences, her mark and the circuit ledger's stamp); Hesk's travel clock (inaccurate; he sets it an hour fast during tournament weeks); a copy of Bracken's sanding habit; currency in marks (he does not spend much). [B4-reconciled 2026-10-05]
editions/monroe-1.3/book-05-the-silver-standard/STATE_LEDGER.md:40:- **Delegation:** two wagons; travel roster of eleven (five competitors, Rooke, Gault, two third-year reserves, a wagoner, and S. Seln for *records and floor scheduling*). The roster line carries the registry name *Caelen Hesk-ward, 41-7843-V* once, so the schedule office's "C. Cael" reads as its abbreviation (§10 item 6). Fourteen of the hill's students are Silver and one is Gold (B4 ch8), and none is fielded; M1 says why in one sentence. Withrow and Bracken travel for the fourth meet and Norhold. Bracken's pouch is the delegation's letter route from Movement 3 on (Karis's information policy). [B4-reconciled 2026-10-05]
editions/monroe-1.3/book-05-the-silver-standard/STATE_LEDGER.md:91:The first day of the qualifying year is day 0 (convocation), after a recess of twelve weeks and four days. No season is named anywhere in this book; weather words only; no month order, month length or cross-month day count is ever stated (OWNER #35, #36.4, #37 O1). Halcenvane's weekdays are the office's First-day … Seventh-day; English names appear only inside Daeva's window at Norhold (#37 O4). The first meet falls about five weeks in, the second about three weeks after it, the third "eleven weeks" after Seln's counter sentence, and the fourth at the year's turn in the deep cold; the road to Norhold runs seventeen days with the melt under the wheels; the tournament runs about three weeks with a rest day at its midpoint (the birthday: seventeen, the eleventh of Sowing by default, never beside a season word; OWNER #35 may move it to "the third of Reaping"). The road home is seventeen days. See `BOOK_MAP.md` §6. [B4-reconciled 2026-10-05]
editions/monroe-1.3/book-05-the-silver-standard/STATE_LEDGER.md:130:**Calendar.** Day 0 is convocation, a First-day; Halcenvane weekdays run First-day … Seventh-day, and Fifth-days fall on days 4, 11, 18 and 25. No season is named. No month is named, and no month order is given. The only date-names in the movement are the B4 recollections (the eleventh of Sowing; the note of the twentieth of Reaping). The first meet falls on about day 35, two days' drive south (the wool town).
