editions/monroe-1.3/book-05-the-silver-standard/state/completion/whole-arc-read.md:145:Not fixed, for the ledger: the landing beat is "three years" at the year's open and "four years" at its close (ch1, ch60), by the map's N9; Withrow's chancellorship is at least eighteen years (ch23, ch28, ch31) beside Book 4's twenty registry years; Vastin's room is nineteen years his; Ephram was two years at the head of the Iron column; the Tide anomaly is touched three times (ch1, ch45, ch60); the office's "three weeks" is the only span given for the sitting; Hesk's clock runs an hour fast from the crossroads to finals morning; the keeper is "he"; Lira's shoulder is the left; the slip count is two; the four initials on the costed rule are in Hesk's book under the minute; the six guesses are written on the night of the closing and Auremont's four words print the morning after; no Norhold session (C8) was drafted, so two renewals stand at the close; Seln's cases are two from fix 6 on, the locked one and a pen-case.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-05-the-silver-standard/state/completion/whole-arc-read.md:150:2. **Economise the exhibition shape (lane A, ch12, ch18, ch21, ch23; lane B, ch51).** Scope: in ch21 the merry Blade to a paragraph and the Log to its bill lines; in ch23 the coastal Wind as it is and the Log to its bill lines; in ch18 the audit to the two rules it adds (the pouch and the closed floors) rather than the whole inventory of what the market holds; in ch12 nothing but the Log; in ch51 the first exchange's recap of the semifinal's shapes to a sentence. Five to nine hundred words in lane A, two to three hundred in lane B. No scene breaks added or removed; no bout cut; the captain and the barge-master untouched.
