editions/monroe-1.3/book-04-copper-crown/state/movement-001/review-cold.md:7:Interest caught immediately on “The pages stopped.” The silence has a physical shape, Prynn's reaction tells me the discovery matters before I understand it, and Karis's refusal to build a house on four uncertain lines establishes both her character and the movement's governing pleasure: proof earned through adversarial care. The legal archaeology is unusually dramatic because it is never merely paperwork; for Cael, an accurate sentence about him is a form of shelter.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-04-copper-crown/state/movement-001/review-cold.md:27:| Character attachment | 9/10 | Chapter 2, Cael realizing careful attention has never before been used “on his own behalf”; Chapter 5, his two signatures on the accurate enrollment | Cael's longing to be described truthfully is understandable even when the law is complex. His refusal to hide uncomfortable facts earns trust, and the friends help without erasing his agency. | High |
