editions/monroe-1.3/book-04-copper-crown/state/movement-006/pre-repair/chapter-41.md:139:"No," she agreed, and nearly smiled. "It's an answer, though. I'm not giving you the number either, because you'll sit on the tier counting, and I'll feel you counting, and it'll be like having a clock in my hip." She shifted the cloth again. "The hip's fine. It's tight. It's been tight since the foundry. Tomorrow it's going to hurt, and the day after tomorrow it's going to hurt more, and then it's going to have nine days, and that's how it's going to be. Nobody's to talk about it."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-04-copper-crown/state/movement-006/pre-repair/chapter-41.md:185:"I'm not thinking about the nineteenth," he said. "Not once. Not until I've beaten him. Every time I think about her, I think about how she moves, and then I'm in a bout with her in my head, and I'm losing to Merrick in real life while I do it." He set his heel again. "So I've decided. Merrick first. Merrick only. If I win, I'll think about her for nine days and not sleep. If I lose, it doesn't matter."
