editions/monroe-1.3/book-05-the-silver-standard/state/movement-001/recheck-r1.md:56:1. **"Thirteen days" — RESOLVED.** ch5 l.131 "*Thirteen days, Karis says, between the response going down and the card coming up. Long enough for an answer. Too long for an easy one.*" Response down d12 (ch4 l.193 "the morning courier of the Sixth-day"); card up d25 (ch5 l.71 "On the Fifth-day"; l.107 "the clean space that had waited there for a fortnight"). Sixth-day to the Fifth-day after next is thirteen. The second sentence is untouched. "Nine days" survives only as Vastin's own nine days of looking (ch5 l.61), which is internal to his window and fits (he receives the file a day or two after d12, looks nine days, sees the card for information on the tenth).
