editions/monroe-1.3/book-04-copper-crown/state/movement-008/recheck-r1.md:91:- **Calendar.** Final the nineteenth (ch52:193), evaluation the twentieth (ch55:265), interview the twenty-first ("Fourth bell today", ch56:19, the day after). Ledger day 21 / day 22 and "thirty-five days since the stair" (ch54:13) follow M7's "day sixteen; twenty-nine since the stair" on the 14th. "Ten days" for the hip (ch51:9; semifinal the ninth). "Nine days" of no sparring (ch51:57). "Eight days ago" (above). "Fourth-days" (ch55:67) is the book's scheme; the 19th is a Fourth-day by the d176 anchor and "they were looked at yesterday" is right for the 20th. No English weekday names, no "weekend", no month order (grep clean).
