editions/monroe-1.3/book-05-the-silver-standard/state/movement-001/review-editorial.md:88:3. **"Nine days" is thirteen on the page (ch5 ¶131).** The response went down "on the morning courier of the Sixth-day" (d12; ch4 ¶199). Hesk's reply comes "the fourth day of the silence" (d16), Lira's wall "the sixth evening" (d18), and the card comes up "on the Fifth-day" with Rooke's targets filling "the clean space that had waited there for a fortnight" (d25; ch5 ¶71, ¶107). Karis's "Nine days … between the response going down and the card coming up" is the map's figure (§6 "about nine days of silence"), not the prose's. Vastin's own "next nine days … On the tenth day" is internal to his window and fine.
