editions/monroe-1.3/book-05-the-silver-standard/state/movement-003/AUTHOR-REPORT.md:45:| 18 | Freight | 5,381 | 5 | **Ephram vs the home Stone (≈1,530):** the sold entry is declined; the Stone takes the stove end and walks Ephram onto the **damp north flags** (0–1); Ephram sees the **heat-shadow** and reads feet below the moving air (1–1); in E4 the Stone walks him north again and his foot travels (1–2); 23 to 24. Ephram's page goes to Lira; she wins the **Iron final** in four, 25 (her third title): "That was your bout. I only fought it." **Brom's final** against the southern boy: **"You fought me. Not the paper."**; 23 to 21; his third title. **Supper:** the board-man in Lira's voice, "Uncertainty is the whole product… I can't chalk a price on a sunrise", **"He's the most classified fighter on this circuit."**; the table laughs. **Ephram's loss itemised like freight**; Rooke's file: *Takes a loss like freight. Ready.*; **Karis's eleven pages** from the panel clerk. Log: the program "from tomorrow it's cover". **The audit, whole company:** what the market has on each of them; thirty feet of a rail; **Bracken's pouch**; **Ephram's entry sold inside a day**; **"Decent and instrumental at once."**; Rooke: "That's cheaper than the lesson I'd have charged for it." **d83 morning:** the slate-country Blade under **item three**, a sharper second exchange, one burst, 2–0; the **Auremont junior writes in his gaps** |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-05-the-silver-standard/state/movement-003/AUTHOR-REPORT.md:46:| 19 | First Installment | 7,196 | 7 | **The grappler foreman (≈2,920):** a Stone, rooting kind; *my lads asked me to*. E1 as designed: he wants Cael, not the cheap touch, and throws him onto slate (0–1); standing slow drains his legs' heat. E2: the feet come back a quarter-beat late; one hand walks wrist→elbow→upper arm into a **lever**; the latch is ready and **kept shut**; the **left shoulder-seam** wrenched; he goes with it, an ugly **knee burst**; no flag. The interval: the bill from the floor, and the foreman standing still. E3 angles and cold (1–1); E4 crowding refused; E5 burst outside the last rush (2–1). "It's only angry." Rooke: "Four days… **Slow on purpose is still slow.** We'll talk about the floor." Lira: **"There's your bill."** Log: two shares plan, one share floor; **"Paid full price, first installment."**; inventory; **the Auremont seam, "Note the sensation. It's been a while."** **Hesk's letter** through the pouch; Lira gets the middle paragraph ("Then he knows I'm loud."). **The quay steps:** Zerin's extract first (read twice: "Everybody goes back to the top"); then the coat-rack account, **"The moment was three years of work, and I already had it."**; the tape-box woman, unnamed; **"Institution's bankrupt; the person gets paid."**; **"She's not faster than me," … "She's faster than me *right now*."** Rooke: **"It's a bracket of ceilings."** **Marek's page:** **"This one's been mispriced too. The dangerous direction."** **d84:** the board shows **26 and 20**; first of six; "Wagons." **Seln's quarterly** (cutaway): **"True. Complete in form. Empty."** |
