editions/monroe-1.3/book-04-copper-crown/state/movement-008/pre-repair/chapter-53.md:235:The three exercises were inside, in the driest hand he owned, every word of them true and none of them complete, each with a tick beside its title and two figures in its margin and an initial on the tab, as the wing marked everything. Something he had never handed in lay against the back board. A slip of paper.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-05-the-silver-standard/manuscript/chapter-27.md:293:At the afternoon halt Cael took Hesk's travelling clock out of his kit and set it forward an hour, as he did in every tournament week. The city was still nine days off, and the clock had been wrong in the ordinary direction since he first owned it, but it seemed to him that the tournament's weeks had begun at that pole.
