editions/monroe-1.3/book-05-the-silver-standard/state/movement-007/AUTHOR-REPORT.md:47:| 46 | The Diagonal | 6,909 | 8 | Auremont's five; Rooke's shortest team talk ("Today somebody counts it"). The presentation: **Daeva looks at the floor, longest at the barrier.** **E1:** "North."; Auremont's pair on the double-cost south platform; Brom in the second gap (a touch; then nobody in blue uses it); Karis's anchored frame at the north-east ramp; Lira's one word, "**Early.**", one burst and a touch. Halcenvane. **E2:** the lattice-breaker walks into the frame until she moves the whole frame to the other ramp; Lira gives Zerin the rail and takes the ground behind; the Silvers refuse the gap and pay in distance; Daeva does her part (one touch on Ephram); **Ephram's trade**, giving away the north-east platform so that two Silvers must hold one beside Brom's gap, "*South.*" Halcenvane, by a handful of quarter-minutes. **Ilsev (≈690):** ten columns and the registry's bracketed word; *Authorizing office: not traced.*; no column for five people doing one thing; her pen stops mid-line; the twelfth chair empty again. **E3:** the read feels weight where there is no body; the **stormlane down the diagonal**; Ephram's call overtaken; Lira early and still too late; the lane passes Brom's gap and **he leaves it by his own judgment**; Karis watches the lane, not her lost frame; the read goes into the air and gives **half a second**; two steps; the lane spends itself beside the oak; **she stops one full second and reads him.** **E4:** they re-form (Brom two strides wide, Karis's frame with a door, Lira "ready, not early"); **Zerin declines an unpriced trade**; Auremont by a few quarter-minutes; 2–2 and the ledger to Auremont; **the Concourse stands**; the frame's empty lines. **After:** Rooke in the tunnel, "**The third exchange wasn't a squad problem.**"; the five-line review sheet; Ephram at the pump (protected 46; "**It had four more sentences and Lira cut them.**"); **protected 25**