editions/monroe-1.3/book-04-copper-crown/manuscript/chapter-05.md:41:He had been keeping the count of days since the gate at Greyvane, every evening, in the margin of the observation notebook. It was five months and nine days, tonight, since a magistrate had stood up in a crowded hall and read him a ruling. He was fifteen years old. He had added the months up twice on the road against Hesk's last letter, because he no longer trusted any number that only he was keeping.
