editions/monroe-1.3/book-04-copper-crown/state/completion/whole-arc-read.md:12:**Rulings on the queued items.** (1) *The baseline month:* the baseline is the forty-eighth day, the second month; ch57, ch61 and ch62 already say so; "first month" for the baseline survives at ch43:201, ch49:195 and fifteen times in ch54–55 and is fixed below (fixes 41, 45, 50–65), six of them to "the baseline" rather than "the second month" so the two chapters do not say "second month" fifteen times. Every other "first month" in the book (the fame tally, Fiske's bouts, the Rooke page, the redirect sequence, the Force girl's habit, Seln's and Cael's first month on the bluff) refers to the term's opening weeks and stands. (2) *#35:* no month order, no month length and no Sowing→Reaping day count appears anywhere; "Sowing" is used only for the eleventh (ch37 ×3, ch62 ×1) and "Reaping" only with its dated days (ch38–59, ch62); the recess and the new month are unnamed; no English weekday name is used at Halcenvane except two in speech (ch7 "I read it on Tuesday", ch12 "Since Tuesday"), fixed below; Greyvane's Thursdays and Wednesdays in ch1–4 match the closed Book 3 and stand. No season is tied to either month; the three season words at Halcenvane ("the spring before last" ch5 ×2 and ch9; "its service in the spring" ch13) are fixed because the ledger's M1 close states "no season named at Halcenvane"; "winter coat" (ch32) and "a winter she could already smell" (ch17) are a garment and a figure and stand, as do the memories of "the first winter at the Ironyard" and "one cold Greyvane winter", which belong to the closed books. (3) *Placeholders:* Gwen (ch31–59) and Abbot (ch24, named once at first meeting and "the Mire boy" after) are used exactly as the rulings ask and are not findings.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-04-copper-crown/state/completion/whole-arc-read.md:17:Checked every dated beat against the ledger's day-numbers and against each other. Greyvane: wk3 the find (Thursday), wk4 nine letters, wk7 replies, wk8 Bracken's four questions on the Wednesday coach, wk11 the forty-one, wk12 the cousin clause, wk14 Thursday the finding, wk16 the transfers, wk17 the fifteenth letter, wk19 the seal, wk20 the rematch, wk21 Thursday Quenna, wk22 Monday Naveth's notice, Wednesday Wray and packing, Thursday Prynn at the gate; four days of road, seven faces, five changes; "five months and nine days" at the bridge (ch5). Halcenvane by the day-count the prose keeps: d2 rooms, d3 the method fails, d6 the yard, d9 Brom assessed, d11 the Log, d13 the hatch, d14 the open session, d19 Withrow, d21 the notice, d22 the first floor hour (twelve days on the bench), "the twelfth of the month" for Lira's signing two days inside the fourteenth (d24), d28 the ladder book, d31 the wall, d32 Karis's terms and eight and nil, d33 the low hall, d34 nine and nil, d35 the late change, d46 the second notice, d48 the baseline, d51 the copying table, d58 29 of 91 and 0 of 7, d66 0 of 31, d68 the empty hall (Seln's post day 23 from d46), d69/d71 the lamp, d73 Sixth-day council, d75 First-day falls, d76 Second-day the wrong issue, d77 Third-day brackets, d79 Fifth-day the revised issue, d80 Sixth-day, four days off three times, d113 Fourth-day the finding, d116 Seventh-day the Mire bout and the counting stopped, d120 the tenth session, d121 the fifth-bell board, the Shield and Tarn and the Current, d133 Third-day the pin ("seventeen days" without counting), d141 Fourth-day the Fiske bout "eight days after the pin", d143 Seln's file "the ninth/tenth night after the pin", d144 the counter "in thirteen weeks" and "eleven days" of two and two, d147 Third-day the first unit and night one, d148 night two, d149 the reach "a quarter of the third hour", d150 the deferral, d154 the misfire "a little over ninety-six hours", d156 Brom's seventeenth, d158–161 the three leaks, d163 the moving half, d164 the coursework "on the fifteenth day", d167 Second-day the eleventh of Sowing with "sixteen days to the final" and the Log's "seventeen days", d168 Third-day the notice, d170 Fifth-day the schedule, d172 Seventh-day the compilation and Withrow's eleven minutes, d173 First-day the ninth of Reaping (file closed, Lira–Fiske), d174 the tenth (Brom–Merrick, "nine days"), d175 the slip, d176 Fourth-day the twelfth (arrival, "seven days… eight"), d177 the thirteenth ("six days"), d178 the fourteenth (hall three, the case home at the sixth bell, ledger day sixteen and twenty-nine since the stair), d179 the fifteenth ("Four days to the final. Five to the twentieth."), d183 the nineteenth (ledger day twenty-one), d184 the twentieth (day twenty-two, thirty-five since the stair), d185 the twenty-first, d186 "third morning of ice", d187 the twenty-third (Lira's four days end at the fourth bell, Cael's three that night), d188 the twenty-fourth ("ten days" after the fourteenth; the posting-house "eight days before" d196), d190 the twenty-sixth quarterly, d191 the twenty-seventh corridor, d196 the last unit, then the fifth, sixth, eighth, tenth, twelfth, thirteenth and fourteenth of the new month. The weekday scheme (First-day to Seventh-day) is consistent from d73 to the end. Hesk's reply on the twelfth to a letter posted the twenty-seventh is a fortnight's round trip to "the far end of the country", which the earlier books' post allows.

