editions/monroe-1.3/book-05-the-silver-standard/manuscript/chapter-60.md:165:He read it again. Then he slid it in behind the old volume's front board, with the other letters that lived there, and ate the stew cold, and did not mind.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-05-the-silver-standard/manuscript/chapter-60.md-166-
