editions/monroe-1.3/book-05-the-silver-standard/manuscript/chapter-57.md:223:He wrote all six into Hesk's book that night, one under another, and drew a line beneath them, and wrote under the line.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-05-the-silver-standard/manuscript/chapter-57.md-224-
editions/monroe-1.3/book-05-the-silver-standard/manuscript/chapter-57.md-225-*Six guesses from a city that has argued about fighters for three hundred years. Every one of them reaches for a shape the world already owns: a secret register, a hidden Path, a cheat, a slip. Not one comes near. What happened doesn't have a shape in anybody's head yet, and you can't guess at a thing you can't picture. Nobody guesses digestion. I'd thought what kept it hidden was us, the four of us and this book. It isn't. It's that nobody can imagine it.*
--
